Homogeneity identity. v_stop(s,a,tau) obeys v(k^2 s, k^2 a... ) -- test the exact
statement instead: at tau = 0, v = sqrt(2 a s) is homogeneous of degree 1/2 in each of
a and s, so e_s = e_a = 1/2 exactly and e_s + e_a = 1. For tau > 0, e_s + e_a is still
1 by Euler's theorem applied to the scaling (s,a,tau) -> (k s, k a, tau) :
  A-33 case 1   s=6 m,  a=20 m/s^2, tau=50 ms  v(ks,ka,tau)= 19.8981  k*v= 19.8981  diff 0.00e+00
