Reading: with a 90 deg untilted forward camera the flight direction leaves the FoV at
1.00 g of braking, capping the usable stop bound at sqrt(2 * 9.81 * 6) = 10.85 m/s,
which is where A-20's success falls to 60 per cent (10 m/s). With the 30 deg up-tilt the
same geometry allows 3.73 g and 21.2 m/s. So s depends on a: ds/da < 0 through body
attitude, and 'relax one limit holding the others fixed' is not an available operation.

